From 377f0c81ec5db519f2e3d6959464558c99df52c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:18:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(doctor): turn the remaining revenue blocker into a
 checklist

Nine patches of funnel work are deployed and the site has taken zero euros,
because /api/pilot-checkout returns 503 to every visitor until Stripe is
configured. That is not a code problem, so no amount of code fixes it.

`pnpm doctor` reads /api/health (which reports configuration presence, never a
secret) and prints what is missing, WHAT IT COSTS while it stays missing, and
the exact fix. Ordered by revenue impact rather than by position in the stack:
four hard blockers where money cannot move, then the degraded set where payment
would work and fulfilment would not.

Exits 1 only on revenue blockers, so it is usable in CI without turning a
fulfilment gap into a red build. Exits 2 when the site cannot be reached.

    pnpm doctor                       # production
    pnpm doctor http://localhost:3000

Verified both ways against a running build: all four blockers reported with
their cost and fix when unset, and a clean "nothing between you and revenue but
customers" plus the Stripe test-mode verification sequence when set.

Evidence: pnpm check clean, 194/194 vitest, doctor exercised in both states.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
